  "id": "Compound::DB00564 - Gene::100861540",
  "verbalization": "Carbamazepine is linked to Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p through a series of indirect pathways involving cytochrome P450 inducers. The evidence suggests that Carbamazepine, as an organonitrogen heterocyclic compound, is included in the inducer group of Cytochrome P450 2c9 and Cytochrome P450 3a4, both of which are known to induce Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p. This induction leads to the binding of these inducers to the target gene, thereby activating the expression of Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p. The presence of Aprepitant, a common inducer of Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p, in multiple pathways highlights a consistent mechanism by which Carbamazepine may influence the expression of this gene. The overlapping pathways and the shared lowest common ancestors underscore a potential mechanism of action that involves the induction of Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p through the interaction with inducer agents, ultimately contributing to the regulation of drug metabolism.",
